C o m p i l a t i o n


      Special-Event Park-and-Ride Planning Problem
      CEE 6410/5410
      David Rosenberg
      October 10, 2026
       
      This problem was contributed by Dr. Ran Sun and expanded by Dr. David Rosenberg
       
      Learning objectives.
      Students will be able to:
      •   Define dimensions, decision variables and an objective function;
      •   Formulate demand, capacity, and service-quality constraints;
      •   Solve a small linear program;
      •   Identify constraints;
       
      Problem Statement
      State Department of Transportation guidance for special events emphasizes advance parklotanning for transportation demand, traffic, parking, transit operations, and seating.
       
      Passengers must also be assigned in full bus-loads of 50 passengers per bus.
       
      Additionally, the event parklotanners must rent and bring in grandstands for the attendees. They have 2 potential venders. Each vender has an up-front reservation cost, number of seats per grandstand, and cost to load, ship, and setup a grandstand.
       
      Vendor  Reservation cost ($)    Seats per grandstand    Cost to load, ship, and setup ($ per grandstand)
      PurpleRain $1,000                   100                 200
      Blue Sky    $1,500                  200                 300
       
      Full details at https://usu.instructure.com/courses/818402/files/100525844?wrap=1
       
      David E Rosenberg
      david.rosenberg@usu.edu
  32   
  33  * 1. DEFINE the SETS
  34  SETS parklot Parking Lots /north, south, west/
  35      vendor Vendors of grandstands /PurpleRain, BlueSky/;
  36   
  37  * 2. DEFINE input data
  38  PARAMETERS
  39     MaxPassengers(parklot) maximimum number of peoparklote parking lot can handle (Number)
  40           /north 600,
  41            south 500,
  42            west  600/
  43     Cost(parklot) cost per passenger from parking lot ($ per person)
  44            /north 4,
  45            south 5,
  46            west  7/
  47     TravelTime(parklot) Travel time from parking lot (minutes)
  48           /north 20,
  49            south 12,
  50            west  8/
  51     MaxAverageTime Maximum average travel time for all pasengers (minutes) /13/
  52     Attendees number of attendees /1200/
  53     ReservationCost(vendor) Cost to reserve grandstands from vendor ($)
  54          /PurpleRain 1000,
  55           BlueSky    1500/
  56     Seats(vendor) Seats per grandstand (number)
  57          /PurpleRain 100,
  58           BlueSky    200/
  59      UnitCost(vendor) Cost per grandstand to load ship and setup ($ per grandstand)
  60          /PurpleRain 200,
  61           BlueSky    300/;
  62   
  63   
  64   
  65  * 3. DEFINE the variables
  66  INTEGER VARIABLES X(parklot), G(vendor);
  67  BINARY VARIABLES I(vendor);
  68  VARIABLES TCOST;
  69   
  70   
  71  * 4. COMBINE variables and data in equations
  72  *EQUATIONS
  73  EQUATIONS
  74      OBJ
  75      Demand
  76      LotCap(parklot)
  77      AvgTime
  78      Seating
  79      UseVendor(vendor);
  80   
  81  OBJ..  TCOST =e= sum(parklot, 50*Cost(parklot)*X(parklot)) + sum(vendor, ReservationCost(vendor)*I(vendor) + UnitCost(vendor)*G(vendor));
  82   
  83  Demand..  sum(parklot, 50*X(parklot)) =g= Attendees;
  84   
  85  LotCap(parklot)..  50*X(parklot) =l= MaxPassengers(parklot);
  86   
  87  AvgTime..  sum(parklot, TravelTime(parklot)*50*X(parklot)) =l= MaxAverageTime*sum(parklot, 50*X(parklot));
  88   
  89  Seating..  sum(vendor, Seats(vendor)*G(vendor)) =g= Attendees;
  90   
  91  UseVendor(vendor)..  G(vendor) =l= ceil(Attendees/Seats(vendor))*I(vendor);
  92   
  93   
  94  * 5. DEFINE the MODEL from the EQUATIONS
  95  MODEL SpecialEvent /ALL/;
  96   
  97   
  98  * 6. Solve the Model as a Mixed Integer Program
  99  SOLVE SpecialEvent USING MIP MINIMIZING TCOST;
 100   
 101   
 102  * 7. Disparklotay the decision variable values in the list file
 103  *DISLAY X.L, I.L, TCOST.L;
 104  DISPLAY X.L, G.L, I.L, TCOST.L;
 105   
 106  * Dump all input data and results to a GAMS gdx file
 107  Execute_Unload "MIP-SpecialEvent.gdx";
 108  * Dump the gdx file to an Excel workbook
 109  Execute "gdx2xls MIP-SpecialEvent.gdx"


